---
/**
 * Sharply seasonal: the November–December spike is most of this page's year, and
 * the buyer is frequently NOT a golfer — which is the segment's core insight
 * (playbook-sim-venue.md §1). So the copy is written for someone buying for a
 * golfer, not for a golfer.
 *
 * ── THE CARD IS TIED TO THE VENUE, AND THAT RESTRUCTURED THIS PAGE ─────────
 *
 * Owner, 2026-09-20: the two venues run SEPARATE Square accounts and a card is
 * only good where it was bought. That is not a detail — it is the first
 * decision the buyer makes, and it cannot be undone once they have paid. So
 * the venue choice comes BEFORE the buy button rather than after it, and the
 * restriction is stated above both, in plain words, where it will not be
 * missed by someone scanning for the orange button.
 *
 * This is also why `global.ts` carries four gift-card URLs instead of two. A
 * shared "check balance" link would answer "no such card" to half the people
 * who used it, and a holder reads that as "my card is void", not "wrong link".
 *
 * ── FOUR GAPS CLOSED, AND ONE CLAIM DELIBERATELY RESTORED (2026-09-20) ─────
 *
 * This page shipped with four `GapCell`s — denominations, whether it covers
 * food and drink, how it arrives, and whether it works at both venues. The
 * owner answered all four, so all four are published facts now and the marks
 * are gone. The page carries no `GapCell` at all any more; do not read that
 * absence as an oversight and do not re-add one without a question to go in it.
 *
 * ⚠️ ONE OF THOSE ANSWERS REVERSES A STANDING INSTRUCTION. The old site claimed
 * a card covered food and drink; the build could find no source for it, marked
 * it as a gap, and left a note reading "Do not put the claim back without a
 * source." The source arrived — the owner, directly, for both venues, on
 * 2026-09-20. The claim is back on purpose and that instruction is discharged.
 * This is written down so nobody finds the old note and strips it out again.
 *
 * ⚠️ Two gift-card vendors were in circulation on the old site — Square on the
 * live pages, Toast on an orphaned old homepage. Square is the one wired up in
 * globalData.external and the one used here. Confirm Toast is dead before launch.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import BookButton from '../components/venue/BookButton.astro';
import StubNote from '../components/venue/StubNote.astro';
import { globalData } from '../data/global';

const metadata = {
  metaTitle: 'Golf Gift Cards — The Links, Lakeville & Stillwater',
  metaDescription:
    'Buy a The Links gift card online for indoor golf in Lakeville or Stillwater, MN. Any amount from $5 to $1,000, good for bay time, food and drink.',
};

/**
 * One array, two venues. Written once so the pair cannot drift — the moment
 * these are two hand-written blocks, one venue gets a correction the other does
 * not, and a wrong Square token on this page takes real money to the wrong
 * account.
 *
 * Each venue's two URLs share a token BY CONSTRUCTION. See the note in
 * `global.ts`: if they ever differ, that is a typo, not a quirk of Square.
 */
const venues = [
  {
    name: 'The Links of Lakeville',
    short: 'Lakeville',
    buy: globalData.external.giftCardBuyLakeville,
    balance: globalData.external.giftCardBalanceLakeville,
    slug: 'lakeville',
  },
  {
    name: 'The Links of Stillwater',
    short: 'Stillwater',
    buy: globalData.external.giftCardBuyStillwater,
    balance: globalData.external.giftCardBalanceStillwater,
    slug: 'stillwater',
  },
];

/** What a card is and does. All verified with the owner, 2026-09-20. */
const theDetails = [
  ['Any amount from $5 to $1,000', 'You choose the figure at checkout rather than picking from a fixed set.'],
  [
    'Bay time, food or drink',
    'It is not restricted to golf. A card can cover a meal and a round of drinks as easily as an hour in a bay.',
  ],
  [
    'A card in hand, or an email',
    'Come in and buy a traditional card if you want something to hand over, or have it sent by email — which is the one that still works on 23 December.',
  ],
];

/** Why this is a good present, written for the non-golfer buying it. */
const whyItWorks = [
  [
    'They do not have to be good',
    'A bay is booked by the hour and the difficulty is a setting. Someone who has never held a club has a decent night; so does a single-figure handicap.',
  ],
  [
    'They pick the night',
    'A bay is booked by the hour, so it fits a Tuesday evening as easily as a Saturday afternoon. Nothing has to be scheduled at the point you buy it.',
  ],
  [
    'It works in February',
    'Which is the point. An outdoor golf gift bought in December is a gift they cannot open for four months.',
  ],
];
---

<BaseLayout metadata={metadata}>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-content px-gutter py-section lg:px-gutter-lg">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold lg:text-5xl">Gift cards</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg text-inkMuted">
      An hour in a bay, a meal, a round of drinks — any amount from $5 to $1,000. They pick the night.
    </p>

    {
      /* 1. THE RESTRICTION, ABOVE THE BUTTONS. It decides which button the buyer
       presses and it cannot be undone after payment, so it does not belong in a
       footnote underneath them. */
    }
    <div class="mt-8 border-hairline border-ink/15 bg-surface p-cell">
      <p class="caps-label text-label-sm text-inkMuted">Choose the location first</p>
      <p class="mt-s3 max-w-prose-page text-body leading-body text-ink">
        <strong class="font-semibold">A gift card only works at the location it was bought from.</strong> Lakeville and Stillwater
        run separate accounts, so a Lakeville card cannot be spent at Stillwater, or the other way round. If you are not certain
        which one they go to, it is worth asking before you buy.
      </p>
    </div>

    {/* 2. Buy and check a balance, per venue, together. */}
    <div id="buy" class="mt-10 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
      {
        venues.map((venue) => (
          <div class="flex flex-col border-hairline border-ink/15 bg-paper p-cell">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">{venue.name}</h2>
            <p class="mt-s3 flex-1 text-inkMuted">
              Sold through Square. Choose an amount and pay; Square handles the rest.
            </p>
            <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-4">
              <a
                href={venue.buy}
                class="inline-block rounded bg-primary px-6 py-3 font-semibold text-surface transition hover:opacity-90"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener"
                data-analytics={'giftcard:buy-' + venue.slug}
              >
                Buy a gift card <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
                <span class="sr-only">for {venue.name} (opens Square in a new tab)</span>
              </a>
              <a
                href={venue.balance}
                class="inline-block rounded border-2 border-current px-6 py-3 font-semibold text-ink transition hover:bg-ink hover:text-surface"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener"
                data-analytics={'giftcard:balance-' + venue.slug}
              >
                Check a balance
                <span class="sr-only">for a {venue.short} gift card (opens Square in a new tab)</span>
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>

    {/* 3. What a card actually is — the four questions that used to be gaps. */}
    <section class="mt-section">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold">What you get</h2>
      <dl class="mt-8 grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-3">
        {
          theDetails.map(([title, body]) => (
            <div>
              <dt class="text-lg font-semibold">{title}</dt>
              <dd class="mt-2 text-inkMuted">{body}</dd>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </dl>
      <p class="mt-8 max-w-prose-page text-inkMuted">
        Anything else — or if you would rather buy one over the phone — either venue will sort it out. The numbers are
        on the <a href="/contact/" class="font-semibold underline">contact page</a>.
      </p>
      <StubNote
        class="mt-6"
        needs="Still to confirm with the client: whether cards carry an expiry, and whether one can be put toward a membership or an hour package rather than spent at the till. Also still open — confirm the Toast vendor on the orphaned old homepage is dead, since Square is the only vendor this page points at. NOTE FOR ANYONE EDITING: the food-and-drink claim on this page is sourced (owner, 2026-09-20, for both venues) and the earlier 'do not put this claim back without a source' instruction is discharged. Do not strip it out again."
      />
    </section>

    {/* 4. Written for the buyer, who often does not play golf. */}
    <section class="mt-section">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold">Buying for a golfer, and you are not one</h2>
      <dl class="mt-8 grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-3">
        {
          whyItWorks.map(([title, body]) => (
            <div>
              <dt class="text-lg font-semibold">{title}</dt>
              <dd class="mt-2 text-inkMuted">{body}</dd>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </dl>
    </section>

    {
      /* 5. Seasonality. The featured-offer slot leans on this in Nov–Dec
       (strategy.md §5) — this section is the landing point for it. */
    }
    <section class="mt-section rounded bg-surface p-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">If it is November or December</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-inkMuted">
        Winter is the season this whole business exists for — league nights, work parties, and no golf outdoors. If you
        are giving one as a Christmas present, suggest they put the date in as soon as they have one, rather than
        leaving it until a Saturday in February happens to be free.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-inkMuted">
        Planning a work party rather than a present? <a href="/events/" class="font-semibold underline"
          >Events and parties</a
        > is the page you want.
      </p>
    </section>

    {/* Every page ends in a transactional CTA (playbook-core.md §6). */}
    <section class="mt-section">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Or just bring them</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-inkMuted">
        A bay is priced by the hour, not the head. Book one and take them with you — cheaper than most presents and you
        get to come too.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4">
        <BookButton size="lg" />
        <a href="#buy" class="font-semibold underline">Back to the gift cards</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
